      "knowledge_point_id": "ec6076ff-1538-5bc0-973d-33d908b0b4d2",
      "knowledge_point": "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression",
      "problem": "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${x}^{2}+11x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}x\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}x+{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{121}{4}.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
